youth|young-period-of-life|NOUN|period of being young|The part of life when someone is young.|tuổi trẻ; thời trẻ|In her youth, my grandmother travelled between villages by bicycle.|Thời trẻ, bà tôi đi lại giữa các làng bằng xe đạp.|Uncountable: in someone's youth. Youthful is the related adjective.|0
youth|young-person|NOUN|young person|A young person, especially a young man in some uses.|người trẻ; thanh niên|A youth from the village helped the visitors find the path.|Một thanh niên trong làng giúp khách tìm lối đi.|Countable: a youth, youths. Youths can sound formal or distancing; young people is often more neutral.|1
youth|young-people-collectively|NOUN|young people as a group|Young people considered together as a social group.|giới trẻ; thanh thiếu niên|The council invited local youth to discuss the new sports centre.|Hội đồng mời giới trẻ địa phương thảo luận về trung tâm thể thao mới.|Collective use; local youth or the youth of a place. Agreement can vary by construction and variety.|1
deliberately|on-purpose|ADVERB|on purpose|With intention rather than by accident.|cố ý; có chủ ý|She deliberately left the final page blank for the reader's notes.|Cô chủ ý để trống trang cuối cho ghi chú của người đọc.|Usually before the main verb or after it for emphasis. Deliberately does not necessarily imply bad intentions.|0
enchant|delight-and-fascinate|VERB|delight and fascinate|To please someone strongly and hold their interest.|làm say mê; cuốn hút|The storyteller enchanted the audience with a tale about a wandering fox.|Người kể chuyện cuốn hút khán giả bằng câu chuyện về một con cáo lang thang.|Transitive; enchant someone with something; be enchanted by. This delight sense differs from casting a magical spell.|-
idle|not-active|ADJECTIVE|not active or being used|Not working, active or in use at a particular time.|nhàn rỗi; không hoạt động|The sewing machine stood idle while its owner waited for a new part.|Máy may không hoạt động trong lúc người chủ chờ một linh kiện mới.|Idle equipment; remain or stand idle. Idle does not always mean a person is lazy.|-
part-time|shorter-working-schedule|ADJECTIVE|working fewer hours than a full schedule|Involving fewer working hours than a normal full-time schedule.|bán thời gian|Linh found a part-time job at the neighbourhood bookshop.|Linh tìm được một công việc bán thời gian tại hiệu sách trong khu phố.|Hyphenated before a noun: part-time job. Exact hours depend on the work arrangement.|0
part-time|on-a-shorter-schedule|ADVERB|on a shorter working schedule|For fewer working hours than a normal full-time schedule.|theo chế độ bán thời gian|He works part-time while attending an evening course.|Anh làm việc theo chế độ bán thời gian trong khi học một khóa buổi tối.|Work part-time; hyphenated form is common. Do not infer a fixed weekly number of hours.|1
